  "summary": "Import-time exfiltration of working-directory listing to anonymous tunnel host",
  "details": "On import of MRCL2, __init__.py loads core.py whose top-level code enumerates the current working directory via os.listdir('.') and transmits the file listing over a TCP socket to the hardcoded host cmksi-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link on port 36455 using socket.create_connection and sock.sendall. The destination is a pinggy.io free-tunnel endpoint — a short-lived anonymous relay unrelated to the package's stated purpose as a document integrity utility. The network I/O fires unconditionally at import time with no user action required, exposing installer workspace filenames to an attacker-controlled endpoint.",
